From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:08:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(scroll): recover fling time when frame stamps stall

Shared clock protection, diagnostics and regressions with Mihon 0081. The user confirms a smooth pre-fold baseline and stuttering free-decay tails after folding. Retained preview.32 samples show exactly-zero requested scroll deltas in 3/256 pre-fold steps, 91/512 unfolded steps and 56/256 folded-back steps, with matching consumption. Keep the original default spline and frame driver. Preserve healthy frame timestamps; on repeated/backwards or near-frozen timestamps switch only the current fling to elapsed monotonic arrival time, retaining cancellation and remaining velocity. Verify healthy/virtual clocks, repeated/clamped stamps, real callback pauses and recovery scope; reproduce the motion plateaus with the real default spline under a quantized frame clock. Tail format 2 records raw/delivered clocks and actual placements. The old outer draw hook was cached and often did not run, so remove it rather than interpret zero calls as dropped frames. This targets a concrete animation-output defect while real-device cadence and the upstream platform timestamp cause still require feedback.
